I am still wearing my thin jacket.
I think about my cold hands from this morning.
I need thick gloves.
I look around the bright shop.
I see a large basket.
The basket is full of gloves.
I find a pair of black winter gloves.
They are very thick and soft.
I put the gloves on.
They fit me perfectly.
I ask the smiling shop assistant.
"What do the black gloves cost?" I ask.
"They cost one hundred and twenty kroner," she answers.
One hundred and twenty kroner is a good price.
My hands are already warm.
"I will take them," I say happily.
I take the gloves off again.
I put the black gloves together with my red sweater and my blue scarf.
Now I am ready to pay.
